"""Final synthesis after all 70 manually assessed bodies; no native execution."""
import hashlib,json,pathlib,runpy
H=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent;P='additional_rust_ooutwire_remaining';runpy.run_path(str(H/(P+'_synthesis04.py')));fs=json.loads((H/(P+'_scope.json')).read_text())['files'];p=H/(P+'.json');r=json.loads(p.read_text())
def e(i,a,b):return {'path':fs[i]['path'],'sha256':fs[i]['sha256'],'lines':[a,b]}
rows=[
('ROUT-F013','high','Unchecked surd products silently change exact values in overflow-unchecked builds','Surd::sqrt forms p*d using unchecked i128 multiplication. The admitted rational r(2^126,5) wraps that product to 2^126, so the result becomes 2^63/5 and its square is only one fifth of the input. Overflow-checked builds panic instead. Radicand multiplication has the same unchecked product pattern; factorization/sign recursion also lack typed work-limit refusal.',[e(15,46,95),e(15,142,156)],'Use checked or cross-cancelled exact products and typed overflow/resource refusal; preserve a round-trip square test at machine boundaries.','ROUT-CHECK016 emulates i128 wrap exactly; no native compilation or profile assumption.'),
('ROUT-F014','medium','Sparse polynomial exponent addition can turn a high-degree product into a constant','Poly2 multiplies u32 exponent keys without checked addition. A one-term x^(2^32-1) polynomial times x has degree zero in an unchecked-overflow profile, or panics when checks are enabled. The example requires only two sparse monomials, not an infeasible dense polynomial.',[e(16,53,58),e(16,112,128)],'Check exponent addition and return a typed overflow, or use an unbounded exponent carrier; validate public canonical-term invariants.','ROUT-CHECK017 independently computes the exact and wrapped degrees; no original execution.'),
('ROUT-F015','medium','Observation presentation admits shape-correct matrices with invalid storage','ObservationPresentation validates edge IDs/domain only, and ObservationMap::observe checks residual shape but omits Matrix::is_well_formed. A public Matrix with rows=cols=1 and empty data can enter a compatible presentation; later observing or inducing a field indexes absent storage. Repair certificate verifiers elsewhere do revalidate storage, so this is a constructor/diagnostic gap rather than a demonstrated false accepted quotient certificate.',[e(2,49,116),e(8,31,75),e(2,572,631)],'Validate matrix storage in observation admission and every public packet boundary before multiplication.','ROUT-CHECK018 isolates the accepted shape and missing storage; indexing failure is source-inferred.'),
('ROUT-F016','high','Lattice admission does not establish its declared one-or-two-local Hermitian premise','LocalHamiltonianTerm fields are public. FiniteQuantumLattice::new delegates to validate_terms, which checks labels, site membership and operator shape, but not support size, repeats, Hermiticity or matrix storage. A public three-site Hermitian 8x8 term on three qubits passes; so does a shaped non-Hermitian one-site packet. The validated helper LocalHamiltonianTerm::new would refuse these. This does not refute the analytic two-local theorem; its premise is not enforced by the accepting API.',[e(13,58,88),e(13,199,244)],'Make fields private or revalidate full term invariants at lattice construction and public mutation/use boundaries.','ROUT-CHECK019 instantiates the exact admission predicate with a complete three-local carrier; no native run.'),
('ROUT-F017','medium','Evolution accepts finite inputs whose phase product becomes nonfinite','For Hermitian H=[2] and finite t=f64::MAX, the exact eigenpair is representable but -lambda*t overflows. evolution_operator calls cis on this nonfinite argument, computes nonfinite diagnostics and returns Ok unconditionally. The preexisting finite-time/eigensolver checks do not establish finite phases or finite unitarity error.',[e(10,463,475)],'Require finite phase arguments and finite output/residual/uncertainty values; return an explicit numerical-domain failure before Ok.','ROUT-CHECK020 confirms IEEE product overflow independently; Rust sin/cos NaN behavior and Ok result are source-based inference, not executed.'),
('ROUT-F018','medium','Nonfinite short-time arithmetic can produce a green bound diagnostic','The signed RHS and margin are not checked for finiteness. With a two-qubit identity Hamiltonian, product |00>, g=1, nu=0 and t=1e200, the analytic defect is zero, the RHS expression overflows to -infinity, and margin>=-tolerance becomes true. This is a vacuous/nonfinite diagnostic, not a counterexample to a finite mathematical lower bound.',[e(13,448,467),e(13,671,682)],'Reject nonfinite derived scalars and state whether a negative finite RHS is merely vacuous; require the advertised time window when claiming a useful lower bound.','ROUT-CHECK021 evaluates the final IEEE expressions only; full native numerical path was not run.'),
('ROUT-F019','medium','Replica exhaustion declaration drops failures and overstates traversed coverage','ReplicaAxiomAudit exposes public flags/counts and certificate() always emits Exhaustion with all-bipartitions wording. It neither binds the family/sample grid nor gates on all_axioms. Failed searches return at the first counterexample, so the emitted record does not prove that every bipartition was inspected. Generic Certificate is already documented as a declaration, so no authenticated proof bypass is claimed.',[e(15,298,332),e(15,592,632),e(28,18,24)],'Retain and bind inputs/results, distinguish successful exhaustive checks from counterexample short-circuiting, and require an explicit result verifier before presenting a proof receipt.','ROUT-CHECK026 plus full search-body review; native tests only cover small fixtures and were not run.'),
('ROUT-F020','medium','Projection CLI can overwrite its reference receipt before detecting failed checks','The --write path writes the newly produced receipt before the later executable_checks_passed failure exit. A failed executable replay can therefore replace the comparison baseline. This audit never invoked the CLI or changed the reference.',[e(7,125,146)],'Gate reference updates on successful checks and use an explicitly reviewed staging artifact or atomic replacement with preserved predecessor hash.','Direct branch-order review; no filesystem mutation probe against original references.')]
d={x['id']:x for x in r['findings']}
for i,s,t,f,ev,a,v in rows:d[i]={'id':i,'severity':s,'title':t,'finding':f,'evidence':ev,'recommended_action':a,'validation':v}
d['ROUT-F012']['validation']='ROUT-CHECK015 independently evaluates all five admitted components, tolerance, assembled_m=5 and reported m_used=0; no native execution.'
