claims=[
{'id':'ROUT-C008','claim':'The exact linear-repair checker binds d0 and omega to a primal residual and a dual annihilator with infinity norm at most one. Equality of primal l1 cost and dual pairing proves optimality for that admitted finite problem independently of search completeness. Cohomology additionally requires a validated d1d0=0 complex and closed omega; positive quotient distance alone is not an H1 class.','evidence':[e(2,154,190),e(2,233,255),e(2,572,631),e(2,700,807)],'dependencies':['Finite rational matrices with consistent dimensions/storage','Exact arithmetic operations return without overflow','Dual feasibility and equal primal/dual objective'],'limitations':['Enumeration is exponential and materializes combinations without a total work budget','Rational i128 operations may panic even where a reduced mathematical answer exists','The two-edge bigon omega=(1,-1) is not closed; the separate three-coordinate example is closed and nonexact','ROUT-CHECK022 is independent arithmetic, not native solver replay']},
{'id':'ROUT-C009','claim':'Contractive observer maps provide real finite passivity and All-Green/joint-kernel checks, with explicit local-to-global refusal when sufficient coverage/injectivity premises fail. Exact coupled-carrier linear algebra shows these edgewise premises are sufficient but not necessary on section-realized defects.','evidence':[e(11,114,129),e(11,145,222),e(11,277,335),e(11,459,478),e(11,659,802)],'dependencies':['Declared observer family and exact defect carrier','Well-formed l1-contractive maps','For coupled sufficiency, defects lie in im(D), not an arbitrary edge product'],'limitations':['No external detector adequacy or physical correspondence is supplied','Scalar tally verify checks internal arithmetic only; source-bound certificates rebuild the family','The coupled result record has public fields and no standalone replay verifier','ROUT-CHECK023 proves displayed finite identities; no new Lean/native execution']},
{'id':'ROUT-C010','claim':'The gauge bridge correctly separates linear coboundary closure, a chosen nonabelian corner polynomial, and group-valued pure-gauge holonomy. It revalidates source inputs before issuing result certificates; orthogonal vertex gauges telescope to identity on explicitly closed contiguous loops.','evidence':[e(6,44,60),e(6,108,138),e(6,231,268),e(6,271,367),e(6,390,501)],'dependencies':['Admitted finite complex d1d0=0','Rational O(n) matrices and consistent dimensions','Declared corners and supplied loops'],'limitations':['A=d0 chi is a linear ansatz, not a nonabelian group pure gauge','Corner indices do not prove a cellular realization, gauge covariance or topology','Three-transition product is a supplied cycle; associated quotient remains an unverified annotation excluded from the certificate','No claim d-squared zero implies exactness, global section existence or absence of nonlinear curvature','ROUT-CHECK024 independently checks the specific finite identities']},
{'id':'ROUT-C011','claim':'The graph retraction onto z=x^2 and exact quarter-turn rotation furnish a concrete counterexample to the projected semigroup law: at (1,0,1), a projected half turn gives (-1,0,1), while two projected quarter turns give (1,0,1). The chart field (x^2,0) is nonlinear.','evidence':[e(16,277,307),e(16,327,395),e(16,397,431)],'dependencies':['This explicitly chosen retraction and ambient rotation','Exact small coefficients/exponents within machine bounds'],'limitations':['This is an example, not a universal projection-obstruction theorem or derivation of a physical theory','Poly2 machine exponent overflow is separately recorded as ROUT-F014','ROUT-CHECK025 is an independent exact construction, not native correspondence testing']},
{'id':'ROUT-C012','claim':'Replica hierarchy code implements distinct finite tests for gauge properties, magnitude sufficiency, disjoint additivity, declared type symmetry and singleton calibration. Pointwise conclusion recomputes singleton decomposition and calibration rather than deriving a universal conclusion from a finite sample grid.','evidence':[e(15,424,480),e(15,592,709),e(15,712,795)],'dependencies':['Admitted finite edges, one-dimensional gauges, sample vectors and scalar list','Correct exact surd arithmetic within supported machine/resource limits','Declared edge-type orbit'],'limitations':['The default nine points and scalars0,1,2 do not establish axioms over all reals','Default distinct edge types can make exchange-symmetry checks vacuous','Public variants and records bypass some constructor validation','Surd overflow and declaration-only exhaustion are material limits, ROUT-F013/F019','ROUT-CHECK026 separates small countermodels only']}]
d={x['id']:x for x in r['claims']};d.update({x['id']:x for x in claims});r['claims']=list(d.values())
vp=H/(P+'_checks04.json');r['validation'].append({'path':'dag/reviews/'+vp.name,'sha256':hashlib.sha256(vp.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'description':'Twelve independent exact/IEEE controls, including valid finite constructions and counterexamples; no native execution.'})
