lines=['# Rust ooutwire source audit','',f"Completed all **70/70** frozen files ({sum(x['line_count']for x in r['file_reviews']):,} lines; {r['scope_bytes']:,} bytes). Every file has a substantive assessment, exact source hash, full line/byte range and reading receipt. Shared boilerplate transfers are explicit and reconstructed byte-for-byte. This closes this slice only.",'','The report contains **12 claims, 20 findings and 26 independent finite controls**. No original Rust/Cargo, provider, private benchmark or historical command was executed. Source tests were read, not rerun.','', 'Useful mechanisms include the primal/dual l1 repair certificate, carrier-bound observer checks with explicit adequacy premises, finite gauge/holonomy checks and concrete projection counterexamples. d1d0=0, closedness, exactness, edge compatibility and global-section claims remain distinct.','', 'Material repair backlog:', '']
